  "stop_criteria": [
    "the parent commit or tree, PR, branch, or draft state drifts",
    "the direct publication scope is not exactly the two additive documentary paths",
    "any product, runtime, dependency, workflow, test, benchmark, or historical evidence file changes",
    "the design describes the existing session lease as absent or reuses it as the global retention-supervisor lease",
    "the existing session lease lacks autonomous owner-fenced heartbeat or can be renewed by reservation or traffic",
    "reserve_batch can create a session or open_session does not atomically create the active row and first durable heartbeat",
    "prepared, reservation, governed transport departure, or feedback publication can succeed with a missing, stale, failed, foreign, or wrong-boot supervisor lease",
    "an expired but unreconciled session can take the normal active-to-closed path",
    "a retention heartbeat can unpause the ledger, refund a budget, acquire a second owner, or renew without a successful retention pass",
    "expiry, scheduler failure, cancellation, split brain, clock rollback, reboot, or storage identity drift can fail open",
    "a redirect, follow-up, pooled client, custom transport, or retry can bypass fresh permit and lease validation",
    "the HTTPX request hook is claimed as the final transport security boundary",
    "the design claims an already-started request can be recalled after the transport-boundary linearization point or claims zero packets after revocation",
    "feedback-store and SQLite lock ordering is ambiguous or inverted",
    "recoverable liveness lapse and permanent integrity fault are conflated",
    "raw task, query, URL, response, participant identity, credential, token, or exception data enters the supervisor audit fields",
    "any provider, search, model, document, benchmark-asset, tester, live-session, or product runtime-network request is required",
    "any retry, authorization label, one-shot A1 rerun, artifact, tag, distribution, release, merge, production action, Phase 11.9, Phase 12, or V1 claim occurs",
    "any ordinary synchronization workflow fails; no rerun is allowed"
  ],
